WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Troubleshooting is a skill, not a guess. We're going to build your diagnostic
process from the ground up.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Common heating failures. No heat from gas furnace: dirty flame sensor (most
common), failed igniter, tripped safety switch, gas valve issue. Read the
control board fault codes first. Furnace short cycling: dirty filter tripping

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Fault Code: LED flash pattern on the furnace control board indicating the
specific failure. Always read codes first.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Winter no-heat calls are urgent. Customers
are cold and stressed. Fast accurate diagnosis builds your reputation.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Read fault codes FIRST on every furnace call. And — Dirty
flame sensor is the number one no-heat cause

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
You get a call — condenser fan not spinning, compressor humming. What's the
first thing you check? Answer that before you move on.

